  description:
  - 'Nutrients are seperated into 3 types: Gloamphage  <sprite name=N_Gloam>, Terrazyme 
    <sprite name=N_Terra>, and Ichor  <sprite name=N_Ichor>. Each plant consumes
    and produces different nutrients, and these nutrients are required for growth.'
  - A tile lacking in nutrients can be restored by either planting a crop that produces
    the desired nutrient, or purchasing fertilizer and applying it to the tile directly.
  - Ichor is a unique nutrient, in that no plant can produce it. The main way to
    restore Ichor to a tile is by defeating a creature nearby the tile. Larger creatures
    produce more Ichor.
  leftText: 'Nutrients are seperated into 3 types: Gloamphage  <sprite name=N_Gloam>,
    Terrazyme  <sprite name=N_Terra>, and Ichor  <sprite name=N_Ichor>. Each plant
    consumes and produces different nutrients, and these nutrients are required for
    growth.'
  rightText: A tile lacking in nutrients can be restored by either planting a crop
    that produces the desired nutrient, or purchasing fertilizer and applying it
    to the tile directly. Ichor is a unique nutrient, in that no plant can produce
    it. The main way to restore Ichor to a tile is by defeating a creature nearby
    the tile. Larger creatures produce more Ichor.
